  "changes": [
    "Replace the complete main-hall bracket kit with genuinely curved incised crossing arms, small receiving dou and closed upper rails. Twenty-eight continuous rising four-stage load paths replace tall pale vertical spacer blocks and meet the original actual roof underside.",
    "Turned wooden capitals carry two narrow inlay rings and twelve small petal plates each. Profile terminals use small paired pierced four-lobed metal fields, exposing timber rather than entire pale end sleeves.",
    "Each stage has an actual perpendicular notched saddle and two connected carved return ribs. Closed pierced spandrels, fitted dark/gilt curved borders and longitudinally recessed main/upper beams complete the post-to-lintel-to-head layers.",
    "The existing independent timber scan supplies normalized grain once; dark beam, warm arm and receiving timber roles are separated from real metal inlays. Original source textures and the same Sun, measured sky, actual unit-gain scene captures, physical camera, exposure and contact pass are held."
  ],
